  },
  "question": {
    "text": "If the parabolas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math> have a common normal, then which one of the following is a valid choice for the ordered triad <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "All of above",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Axis of both parabola is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p><p>As we know, axis of parabola is always a normal to the parabola.</p><p>Hence, for all values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> a common normal is present.</p><p><strong>Another Method:</strong><br />Normal to parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is give by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>Normal to parabola</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>replacing</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>by</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>by</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>and normal to parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>replacing</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>by</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>]</mo></math></p><p>For common normal, we should have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>[using Equations. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>]</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>As, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Note that if&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then all options satisfy (: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is a common normal).</p>"
  }
}